In this pull request I achieved the next goals:
1. A React/Redux app that fetches information about the top 100 cryptocurrencies;
2. React is based on 7 components;
3. Currency component for displaying a link to each currency;
4. Footer/Navbar for displaying footer and navbar of the page;
5. Search form that has a filter by name and symbol for searching through the list of currencies and display it filtered;
6. CurrenciesContainer for displaying the list of links of currencies;
7. DetailedCurrency for displaying all the data about 1 currency;
8. A Redux reducer with actions for fetching data from Nomics API, show one currency and filter them by name and symbol;
9. Routes for two components: CurrenciesContainer for all the currencies and DetailedCurrency for displaying each of them;
10. CSS styles for all of them;
11. Jest and React Library tests for all components, reducer, and API.

P.S. I want to mention a very important detail, in order to use this API from another domain except for localhost, it is needed to be accepted by Nomics support. So, I am receiving a cors error at this point on Heroku because I am waiting for their approval.
Any way you can run the app on localhost and it will work perfectly.

